3. The Annual Report notes the implementation of new accounting standards: "IAS 33 Earnings per share and IFRS 8 Operating Segments have been applied in these interim financial statements... Prior period information has been amended to reflect the requirements set out in IAS 33 and IFRS 8."

### 3. Additional context (if relevant):
The discrepancies are minimal (between 307.548 million, 307.549 million, and 307.941 million NOK) and represent a variance of less than 0.13% at most. These differences are likely due to final audit adjustments, rounding, or minor reclassifications rather than material restatements of financial information.

No historical EBITDA figures for 2017-2018 were found beyond what was already known (212.370 million NOK for 2018 and 139.988 million NOK for 2017), and no additional reconciliation tables for these years were located in the documents.

The company underwent significant changes including an IPO in October 2020, which may have led to refinements in how certain financial metrics were presented. The differences appear to be non-material from an investor perspective, as they don't materially change the financial picture of the company's performance.
